The latest review isolates one remaining defect: after an upload-source timeout, the public call can resume before cooperative timeout children have retired, so ownership snapshots are order-sensitive. I’m reproducing that exact combined test gate and then I’ll tighten the timeout-race handoff so cancellation/retirement state is deterministic while a truly cancellation-ignoring source remains visibly owned.
