 ## 2026-08-10
 
+### 2144 — libssh2 upload timeout exposes deterministic ownership (TASK-260715-1ozsb6)
+- ROOT CAUSE: The timeout race resumed its public continuation before cancelling the losing child, and the upload path returned after cancelling cooperative stdout/stderr work without waiting for those timeout-race records to retire. Depending on scheduling, the post-timeout snapshot contained the one intentionally non-cooperative upload source plus transient cooperative children; an unbounded test poll could then turn the ownership mismatch into a hung combined gate.
+- REWORK: The race now signals cancellation before resuming its caller. The bounded ownership registry supports count-targeted retirement waiters, and a timed-out upload gives cooperative children at most 250 ms of the injected close budget to reconcile while permitting exactly one additional operation—the cancellation-ignoring source—to remain visible until release. The regression uses bounded monotonic state synchronization and fails instead of hanging if ownership cannot settle.
+- VERIFICATION: The formerly order-sensitive `swift test --filter LibSSH2` gate passed three consecutive stress runs and a final post-edit run (41 tests/3 suites each). `make validate-core` passes 375 tests/31 suites plus boundaries and build; `make validate-libssh2`, `make test-libssh2-source-gates`, `make native-apple-matrix`, strict recursive Swift format, and `git diff --check` all exit 0. Board validation exits 0 while retaining the known `STORY-260715-lkshfz` aggregate mismatch as visible evidence.
+
 ### 2112 — libssh2 teardown reconciles reserved races and late automatic-task retirement (TASK-260715-1ozsb6)
 - ROOT CAUSE: A reserved timeout race resumed teardown after its first child resolved but remained registered until both children retired. Teardown exposed completion without draining that registry, and it did not arrange durable automatic-task retirement until after socket close; if a cancellation-ignoring socket consumed the close deadline, the join branch was skipped and completed automatic-task references remained permanently counted.
 - REWORK: Automatic-task retirement now starts before socket close and clears actor-owned references only after every cancelled task actually returns. The reserved registry is drained within the existing close deadline, so cooperative races reconcile before completion while genuinely non-cooperative socket work remains visible until its safe late return.
